  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "x8ZOS5Gp5D0Y7nCqN8vsi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2486.088200729304,
      "y": -1111.8662881633807,
      "width": 737.679443359375,
      "height": 1280,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aY",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 656896084,
      "version": 2834,
      "versionNonce": 366848100,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1751777031363,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n\nFunctional Requirements: \n- Want to send notification of different types like email, phone message etc, easily extendible \n- Want to send the immediate as well as schedule notifications, also \n  recurring notifications. \n\n\nNon- functional Requirements: \n- Idempotent and exactly one delivery.\n- Logging \n- Alerts and monitoring\n- Very high scalable.\n- Error handling.\n- Fault tolerance and reliable.\n\nEstimations: \n-  QPS -> 10k , including all messages. \n-  Read:Write -> 1:10 -> 1000 qps for read. \n- qps ratio for immediate, recurring or schedule\n-  Storage -> Later\n\nEntity: \n- NotificationRequest, ScheduledNotification, execution. \n\n Api Design: \n\n 1. immediate notification; https, grpc\n\n/api/v1/notification/immediate   POST\n\nheader -> x-token or sessionId,  \n             x-track-id: <>\n\n Request: \n     \n   {\n      type: IMMEDIATE, SCHEDULE, RECURRING\n      time: \n      recurringType: WEEKLY, HOURLY, DAILY  \n      payload: <>\n      requestType: // EMAIL, MESSAGE...\n \n   }\n\n Response: \n\n   {\n       statusCode: <> \n       responseId: <>.  // can use for polling to check status\n   }\n\n2. Polling the notification status\n\ngrps, https: \n\n/api/v1/notification/status ? id = <>.   GET\n\nResponse: { \n  Id: <>\n  Status: <>. // FAILED, SUCCESS, PENDING\n\n}\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n\nFunctional Requirements: \n- Want to send notification of different types like email, phone message etc, easily extendible \n- Want to send the immediate as well as schedule notifications, also \n  recurring notifications. \n\n\nNon- functional Requirements: \n- Idempotent and exactly one delivery.\n- Logging \n- Alerts and monitoring\n- Very high scalable.\n- Error handling.\n- Fault tolerance and reliable.\n\nEstimations: \n-  QPS -> 10k , including all messages. \n-  Read:Write -> 1:10 -> 1000 qps for read. \n- qps ratio for immediate, recurring or schedule\n-  Storage -> Later\n\nEntity: \n- NotificationRequest, ScheduledNotification, execution. \n\n Api Design: \n\n 1. immediate notification; https, grpc\n\n/api/v1/notification/immediate   POST\n\nheader -> x-token or sessionId,  \n             x-track-id: <>\n\n Request: \n     \n   {\n      type: IMMEDIATE, SCHEDULE, RECURRING\n      time: \n      recurringType: WEEKLY, HOURLY, DAILY  \n      payload: <>\n      requestType: // EMAIL, MESSAGE...\n \n   }\n\n Response: \n\n   {\n       statusCode: <> \n       responseId: <>.  // can use for polling to check status\n   }\n\n2. Polling the notification status\n\ngrps, https: \n\n/api/v1/notification/status ? id = <>.   GET\n\nResponse: { \n  Id: <>\n  Status: <>. // FAILED, SUCCESS, PENDING\n\n}\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
